WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.626
Local inference can reduce dependence on external model services,

00:00:03.626 --> 00:00:05.585
but privacy still requires design.

00:00:05.585 --> 00:00:08.719
Data boundaries include more than the prompt box.

00:00:08.719 --> 00:00:13.029
Files, attachments, chat histories, local logs, screenshots, exports, backups, shared folders,

00:00:13.029 --> 00:00:16.947
and connected tools can all carry information from the workflow.

00:00:16.947 --> 00:00:20.082
Before a workflow is repeated, classify the data.

00:00:20.082 --> 00:00:23.216
Public information, internal notes, project-confidential material, personal data,

00:00:23.216 --> 00:00:24.783
customer data, regulated data,

00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:27.917
and sensitive operational details may require different handling.

00:00:27.917 --> 00:00:31.444
Some data may be fine for a local session.

00:00:31.444 --> 00:00:35.753
Other data may need redaction, approval, or a different workflow entirely.

00:00:35.753 --> 00:00:40.063
Do not assume every local workflow is safe for every dataset.

00:00:40.063 --> 00:00:45.548
A model session may be local, but the output may be copied into email,

00:00:45.548 --> 00:00:47.899
documents, source control, tickets, or chat.

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:49.466
Backups may sync files.

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:52.209
Logs may preserve prompts or response fragments.

00:00:52.209 --> 00:00:56.910
A useful boundary follows the data after the model response is generated.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.086
Retention choices matter.

00:00:58.086 --> 00:01:02.395
Decide which prompts, outputs, settings, and exported files should be kept.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.922
Remove temporary material when it is no longer useful.

00:01:05.922 --> 00:01:10.623
Keep important records only where they belong and where access is appropriate.

00:01:10.623 --> 00:01:12.974
Privacy is both technical and behavioral.

00:01:12.974 --> 00:01:16.892
Device security, file permissions, workspace separation, redaction habits, cautious sharing,

00:01:16.892 --> 00:01:20.026
and clear review rules all support sovereign AI.

00:01:20.026 --> 00:01:24.728
The safest local workflow is explicit about what data enters, what leaves,

00:01:24.728 --> 00:01:26.295
and what remains stored.

00:01:26.295 --> 00:01:31.780
When the boundary is unclear, pause and decide before adding more files or automation.
